# The SHA-256 of every file in the Packages directory of a retail Mac OS X
# 10.6 Snow Leopard install DVD, one disc per "# build" section. The plugin
# never downloads a disc: the user supplies an image of their own, and
# internal/disc.Verify holds the volume inside it to these values, so any
# faithful copy passes whatever tool made the image. A build may have more
# than one disc, each its own section under the same "# build" line; a
# volume passes when it matches any one of them.
#
# build 10A432, the first section (10.6.0 retail, the full DVD; its tell is
# UserDVDMask.bom): read 2026-10-04 inside the privops microVM
# (assets/privops/disc/verify-disc.sh) from an ISO of 7,771,521,024 bytes,
# sha256 cbeeb2378c40b20a9b06236f567de593e9030a0a865515b50cf6d35833e25cd5,
# whose HFS+ volume starts at byte 1,034,489,856; BSD.pkg, OSInstall.mpkg
# and AddressBook.pkg read again on the host with 7-Zip, which shares no
# code with the Linux hfsplus driver, and agreed.
#
# build 10A432, the second section (10.6.0 retail, the Upgrade DVD; its
# tell is UpgradeDVDMask.bom in place of UserDVDMask.bom, and not one of its
# 281 sums is the first disc's): read 2026-11-19 inside the privops microVM
# (assets/privops/disc/verify-disc.sh) from a UDIF .dmg of 5,602,561,340
# bytes, sha256 4f1ae6edd30eabbd8becc1227414d45098741d6b477a6d44cff3d1b244c4a346,
# whose HFS+ volume dmg2img writes out at 6,736,879,616 bytes; all 281
# read again on the host with 7-Zip 23.01, and agreed.
#
# A disc of another build, or another disc of a known build, is added as
# its own section once one has been read the same way.
#
# build 10A432
